    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partners Gill & Glynn are delighted to present No. 25 Hazel Court, a spacious four-bedroom semi-detached residence extending to approximately 118 sq. m. (1,270 sq. ft.), ideally located within the popular Hazel Court development on Convent Road, Ballinrobe.\n\nHazel Court is a well-established residential development with attractive green areas throughout and is within walking distance of Ballinrobe town centre and a host of local amenities, including schools, shops, restaurants and recreational facilities.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nAccommodation extends to approximately 118 sq. m. and briefly comprises an entrance hall, spacious sitting room with feature stone fireplace and solid fuel stove, kitchen/dining area with extensive fitted units and tiled flooring, utility room and guest WC.\n\nThe first floor provides four well-proportioned bedrooms, including a master bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom and hot press. The bedrooms benefit from built-in wardrobes and ample storage throughout.\n\nThe bright and well-maintained accommodation benefits from attractive timber flooring in the entrance hall, sitting room and bedrooms, while the kitchen and bathrooms are tiled.\n\nThe property is heated by oil-fired central heating, with radiators throughout. Its boasts a B3 BER energy rating making it eligible for green finance and low energy running costs.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a tarmac driveway to the front providing off-street parking, with a lawned area adjoining. \n\nTo the rear is a private, enclosed garden, laid mainly in lawn and complemented by mature planting. \n\nA new (4 metres X 3 metre) steeltech shed will also form part of the sale together with some furniture. \n\nLOCATION\n\nThe property is ideally situated within Hazel Court, a popular residential development on the edge of Ballinrobe town. The town offers a wide range of amenities including supermarkets, shops, cafés, traditional and modern public houses, restaurants, schools and childcare facilities, all within easy reach of the property.\n\nBallinrobe is renowned for its excellent sporting and recreational facilities, with Ballinrobe Racecourse and Ballinrobe Golf Club located nearby. The town also benefits from its proximity to Lough Mask, Lough Corrib and Lough Carra, making the area particularly attractive to anglers and outdoor enthusiasts.\n\nBallinrobe is approximately 30 miles from Galway City and within easy commuting distance of Castlebar, Westport and Ireland West Airport Knock.\n\nNo. 25 Hazel Court represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a spacious four-bedroom family home in a well-established and convenient residential development.\n\nVIEWING\n\nProperty Partners Gill & Glynn strives to be ultra flexible around property viewings.\nTo arrange a viewing, call, or text/WhatsApp Claire Glynn on 087 965 5584 or call 091 884000.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only.\n"
      },
      {
